Z||000005||batboy||10-21-2000||08:08 PM||||Chad, maybe I am FINALLY growing up. Johnny, nope...it's a GT, but not the supercharged GTP. Although, I did look at a couple GTP along the way. The used ones usually have been rode hard and put away wet. Since I have several hotrods, including the Batmobile, I decided I didn't need an extra 40 ponies to get me into trouble. Well, here's my new "babe magnet" looking pretty. She has every available option except power lumbar, heated seat, and alarm.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GP-98-GT-nice.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000006||batboy||10-21-2000||08:11 PM||||"Wanna race?"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GP-98-GT-F4.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||10-21-2000||08:43 PM||||Those motors fit nicely into Fieros you know.||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||10-21-2000||09:43 PM||||Phil, shhhhhh, don't tell anyone, but when I trade this Grand Prix in on a new one in a couple years, it just might have a tired ol' 2.8 engine under the hood and the original 3800 might find it's way into a Fiero. LOL! Well, it's a nice dream.<P>Gawd forbid and knock on wood, but if this car ever gets totaled out, I am keeping the drivetrain, all joking aside! The 3800 has got to be one of the best engines GM is producing right now.<P>I did look at a couple Oldsmobile Intrigues with that new 3.5 all aluminum engine. They have more power than the normally aspirated 3800 and are lighter weight. I don't know how well they hold up in the long run, but they might be a possible engine swap candidate. The 3.5 V6 is a similar design to the NorthStar V8.<P>However, beginning in 1999, the Grand Am GT and the Olds Alero (equipped with the bigger optional engine) are using the new high tech 3400 engine that might be ideal for the Fiero. It's the tried and true 3.4 block with special heads and overhead cam. GM may of finally figured out how to build a dependable overhead cam engine...finally. In a couple more years, there will be a lot of those engines available in wrecked cars.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||10-22-2000||08:18 AM||||<B>Very</B> nice car, bb.  Congrats.<P>As for the lack of a few minor options:<P>"Power lumbar"?  Who's gonna be driving your new beast other than you?  Set it and forget it.<P>Heated seats are overrated.<P>And you can always install an aftermarket alarm on your own.<P>What was that gray, metallic thing that said "USAir Farce"?  I know.  It was a Delorean, wasn't it?  You can take him! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
