Z||000016||batboy||10-24-2000||08:51 PM||||It didn't take any funds. I shopped around for almost 2 months until I finally found a super nice car at a bargain price. Then, my credit union bought me the car and I just make a whole bunch of monthly payments. Deep in debt, it's the American way!<P>By the way, I found my GP through autotrader.com and I thought it was a very handy way to look for a car. The seller pays for the ad, so the buyers get to look at anything on the site free of charge. You can restrict your search to specific models of cars, price range, and distance from your zip code. I don't own any stock in them either.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000017||frontal lobe||10-25-2000||12:12 AM||||Congratulations on the car.  It looks really nice.  I think you made a wise choice to not go for a car that would have put you many thousands further in debt.  You are going to enjoy this one a ton anyway.<P>I love autotrader.com, too.  I found my wife's miata that way.  I can blow a lot of time on there just dreaming.  Saw a v8 Fiero on it a few months ago and if I could have sold my Fiero, I would have got it.<P>I agree with Monkeyman, heated seats are over-rated.  I have lots of use for them living in Wisconsin.  I have them in my Millenia (of course it's the S version, otherwise why get one?).  My butt warms the seat up before the seat-warmer, and then I forget it's on.  So finally I'm getting a "hot seat" and wonder why and remember,  "Oh yeah, I turned on the seat-warmer", and shut it off.  Very wierd.||||reg||1
